Accept partitioning results that differ from the stored answer files when
they are still valid and good. The tests compare zdrive's output with
answer files made with older METIS, ParMETIS and Scotch versions; newer
versions give different, equally valid partitions and orderings.

When an output differs, check that it covers the same objects as the
answer. Orderings must be permutations. Partitions must use the requested
parts and, measured on the test's Chaco graph, have a max part load
(per weight) and an edge cut within ZOLTAN_TEST_LOAD_MARGIN (default
1.15) and ZOLTAN_TEST_CUT_MARGIN (default 1.30) of the stored answer.
Drop-test outputs must still match exactly.

